    "created_at": "2016-05-09T08:59:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-05-09T08:59:37Z",
    "body": "`allow-top-navigation` doesn't really matter here, because that only affects navigation of our own top.\n\n> What happens if the window.open is targeting an already-existing window (possibly including the one it opened with allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox)?\n\nI'm pretty sure this will fail in Gecko (once implemented), if we try and re-navigate a sandbox escaped window that we opened, but we don't get set as the one permitted sandboxed navigator.\n",
