    "created_at": "2016-09-07T20:48:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-07T20:48:37Z",
    "body": "OK, if I read https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src.git/+/55.0.2852.1/third_party/WebKit/Source/core/frame/Frame.cpp#198 correctly then Chrome basically skips https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#allowed-to-navigate step 3 if `A` doesn't have the \"sandbox propagates to auxiliary browsing contexts\" flag set or something.  That seems like a nasty hole for cases like this:\n\n```\n<a href=\"http://example.com\" target=\"foo\">Click me first</a>\n<iframe srcdoc=\"<a href='http://evil.com' target='foo'>Click me second. Did I navigate?</a>\"\n        sandbox=\"allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox\">\n</iframe>\n```\n\nin that it allows the sandboxed thing to navigate a window it has absolutely no relation to.  In particular, it allows the sandboxed page to attack the parent page by navigating things out from under it.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
