    "created_at": "2016-09-07T22:05:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-07T22:05:47Z",
    "body": "So the spec seems to have somehow two definitions when 'one permitted sandboxed navigator' is set.\n\"If the current browsing context's active document's active sandboxing flag set has both the sandboxed navigation browsing context flag and sandbox propagates to auxiliary browsing contexts flag set ... the current browsing context must be set as the new browsing context's one permitted sandboxed navigator.\"\n\nand \n\"If the sandboxed auxiliary navigation browsing context flag is not set, then in certain cases the restrictions nonetheless allow popups (new top-level browsing contexts) to be opened. These browsing contexts always have one permitted sandboxed navigator, set when the browsing context is created, which allows the browsing context that created them to actually navigate them.\"\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
