    "created_at": "2016-09-09T13:48:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-09T13:48:09Z",
    "body": "I apologize that I didn't follow up on this either. I need to do a better job at paying attention to these questions.\n\nhttps://output.jsbin.com/jimoqe shows that your analysis is correct, and Chrome does the wrong thing when navigating targeted windows. I agree that that's not the intent of the feature, and setting the \"one permitted sandbox navigator\" for popups created from a frame with this sandbox flag seems like a reasonable way of approaching the problem. I filed https://crbug.com/645450 to cover it.\n\nI think we can address this in the spec by changing step 5 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#the-rules-for-choosing-a-browsing-context-given-a-browsing-context-name to something like:\n\n> If the current browsing context's active document's active sandboxing flag set (<var>set</var>) is not empty, andthe chosen browsing context picked above, if any, is a new browsing context, then:\n> 1.  If <var>set</var> has the sandboxed navigation browsing context flag, then the current browsing context must be set as the new browsing context's one permitted sandboxed navigator.\n> 2. Unless <var>set</var> has the sandbox propagates to auxiliary browsing contexts flag, all the flags that are set in the current browsing context's active document's active sandboxing flag set when the new browsing context is created must be set in the new browsing context's popup sandboxing flag set.\n\nDoes that seem reasonable?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
